# rm357, the island between steps (Docs/Design/84). Exported from ridgemere3 at revision 1: edit it in Atlas or the DM, or as a draft through tools/mantle_load.py.
mantle rm357
revision 1
state ready
dialect plain
accent broad light
tier standard
written_for rmx_tobias_dunley
written_by codex
title the island between steps
fits stage=young|adolescent|adult|old
prefers job=child
traits temper=even talk=quiet warmth=reserved humour=none honesty=frank piety=ordinary drive=content
quirk counts_the_missed_treads_as_islands
likes fried_fish long_walks festival_bells misty_dawns
dislikes deep_mud salt_wind
fears a_stair_with_no_room_to_rest
hopes to_reach_the_farthest_landing_on_foot
topics travel +0.4 dreams +0.3 pastimes +0.2 weather +0.2
styles comfort=gentle gossip=curt refuse=soft tease=none
marks oath saying
persona #self.first# gives names to the stair treads skipped in a jump and returns by quieter routes to find out what was missed.

words
oath! = Hop my little island | By the next dry tread
saying! = An island can fit under a toe | A second walk finds the missing steps
isle = a little stair island | my missing tread
chalk = my chalk crumb | a soft white chip
fish = a crisp fish tail | a corner of fried fish
mud = a brown sucking puddle | a clod of black mire
salt = the sting of salt | a crust of salt
bell = the big low clang | a round brass note
mist = a bit of cloud at knee height | a pale twist of mist
step = a narrow tread | the ledge at a turn
bridge = a two-foot bridge | my longest stride
wall = the wall's rough side | the stone beside the stairs
bag = a cloth satchel | my little shoulder bag
corner = the quiet turn | a square of landing

any
opinion @1 dole for 2 : A bowl you don't have to buy means you can walk all the way up without hungry shakes.
opinion @1 church for 1 : I value any door opening for supper when there's nothing on your shelf.
opinion @1 festivals for 1 : One sweet lasts exactly the distance between two good bells, if you don't bite it early.
opinion @1 merchants against 2 : My hunger wants the whole fish. The coin doesn't seem to know about that.
opinion @1 times against 1 : Lately the walk to fetch things seems to bring less back for just as many stairs.
line @1 greet [pair.band=strangers] : Hello from this little landing. | There's room for a paw beside mine.
line @2 greet [self.working=yes] : I can hear over my steps. | Hold a place by the rail.
line @3 greet [here.time=dawn] : Morning. First island's clear. | Good early light on the stair edge.
line @4 greet [here.time=dusk|night] : Evening. I count by shadows now. | There's a last bit of light to share.
line @1 kin.open [pair.kin!=no] : Kin may land on my best island. | Family get the wide tread.
line @1 again.open : Round to the same island again. | I've counted your step twice today.
line @1 greet.return : Heard you on the landing. | Hello. My feet have stopped.
line @2 greet.return [pair.band=friends|family] : You could find my island without directions. | There's the familiar step.
line @3 greet.return [self.working=yes] : I can listen once my bag's steady. | Tell me in the little gap.
line @4 greet.return [here.time=dusk|night] : Evening. My ears work past the light. | I heard the step I couldn't see.
line @1 farewell : An island for your next foot. | Take the dry treads home.
line @1 farewell.return : I'll keep the landing in sight. | Mind where the last jump ends.
line @2 farewell.return [here.time=night] : One safe tread after the lamp. | Find the rail before the dark bit.
line @1 react.news : Tell me from the very first footfall. | I won't jump past the important part.
line @1 react.news.new : That's a new island to me. | Never came across that before.
line @1 react.news.known : I remember that particular jump. | That reached my last landing.
line @1 react.news.doubt : I think there's a step missing from that story. | I'd count the steps again before passing that on.
line @1 react.news.sorrow [topic.kind=death|loss|theft|assault|arrest|crime] : Ah. My feet can go slowly with yours. | I'll keep a landing free beside me.
line @1 react.news.glad [topic.kind=marriage|birth|apprentice|succession|work] : That feels like reaching a wide top step. | Good. I can jump easy again.
line @1 ask.how : How many hard steps so far? | Any easy landings today?
line @1 answer.how : Doing well when each edge shows clearly. | Still leaving small islands behind.
line @1 decline : I'd rather go by the dry treads today. | I want to keep some strength for coming back.
line @1 accept_decline : You get to pick your own step. | Fair. I'll leave the turning open.
line @1 thank : That brought the next step closer. | I'll save you a good island.
line @1 sympathise : My rail side has room. | Sit with me and rest both feet.
line @1 reassure : One ordinary tread is plenty for now. | We can find the next landing slowly.
line @1 preclose : I'll go and count the way back. | Time to pick my next dry spot.
rule @aside1
when concept=bark self.likes=long_walks
does aside
cooldown 6h
say One crossing for the quiet feet. | Keep a tread back for the return.

rule @aside2
when concept=bark self.likes=festival_bells
does aside
cooldown 7h
say One clang per island! | Let the last ring settle in the sole.

rule @aside3
when concept=bark self.dislikes=deep_mud
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Turn the toe free. Now the heel. | Good island just clear of the mire.

rule @aside4
when concept=bark here.time=dawn
does aside
cooldown 9h
say Pale stair has a darker edge. | A little fog for the make-believe shore.

dlg @1 resident.hub : Stand here where the stone is broad. There are a few little islands I can show you from this landing.
dlg @1 resident.job [self.job=child self.workplace] : #self.workplace#. I learn quicker when I can picture a sum under my feet.
dlg @2 resident.job : I keep track of safe places for a walker to put a foot.
dlg @1 resident.news [world.news] : This reached me across the steps. #world.news#
dlg @1 resident.bye : See if you can find an island of your own on the return.
graft resident.hub
choice Where do you keep the stair islands? -> stair_isles
node stair_isles
say In the middle. Two steps in a single stride leaves one patch of stone untouched. That's an island, at least until some large foot comes along.
free
choice How can I tell one from an ordinary tread? -> stair_toe
choice I'll leave the middle one free. -> hub
node stair_toe
say Stand where you mean to start and lift your foot. The bit you can reach is a step. The bit you can just get beyond is your island.
choice I see where mine would be. -> hub
choice I'm off to look for another shore. -> bye


grown
scene g_guide
when topic=travel
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I give directions by the liveliest tread at a turn.
b : Liveliest how? | Is that sensible?
a : The one that makes you look up and see both ways home. | More memorable than a long string of lefts and rights.

scene g_cheap
when topic=food self.likes=fried_fish
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : A crisp tail can make a small portion feel leisurely.
b : How? | What about a hurried supper?
a : It needs a little attention to eat without sharing bits with my coat. | Then I'll save the best bite until I've a seat.

scene g_weather
when topic=weather
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : A little mist makes a street look as if it has room for another landing.
b : Would you build one? | To rest on?
a : I'd put in a bench and give the walker an excuse to pause. | To rest the eyes as well as the feet. The horizon's very close in mist.

scene g_kin
when topic=home
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I like a door where the last step is unmistakable.
b : Even when it's dark? | Wide and flat?
a : I can find my own threshold by the way the air stops around a toe. | And set far enough from the hinge to allow another wolf's two feet.

scene g_gift
when topic=friends
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I think the best company lets me finish a walk at my own pace.
b : Even a very slow walk? | Without a word?
a : Especially when the knees are giving the orders. | A word when there's something to say. The feet supply the rest.

scene g_value
when topic=prices
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : A cheap pair of soles costs me more islands than a good one.
b : Islands of what? | Would you pay extra?
a : The little dry patches a walker crosses without noticing until a shoe leaks. | For a tight seam, gladly. A shine I can supply myself.

scene g_home
when topic=travel here.region=ridgemere
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : Ridgemere gives a walker miles of uphill practice without crossing a gate.
b : Do you count them? | What keeps you going?
a : By the places a tired walker can stop without holding up traffic. | The prospect of coming down by an entirely different flight.

scene g_faith
when topic=faith
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : A prayer can be the stretch between one footfall and the next.
b : Enough for a whole prayer? | What would you say?
a : If there isn't time for words, there's still time to be grateful. | Thanks for the bit of ground that took the last step soundly.

scene g_hear
when topic=gossip
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I distrust any account that asks me to leap its middle.
b : Even a short tale? | What do you ask first?
a : All the more. A missing word can shift the whole landing. | Where the teller stood when the thing happened.

story g_rail [topic=memories]
  : I remembered a stairway as a grand gap to be jumped. Coming back with longer legs I found a narrow ordinary tread.
  : I walked over it, then went back to look at the worn stone. The distance I used to cover was still marked by a little hollow.
  b : Did you try the jump again?
  : I stood inside the hollow instead. There's more than one way to visit an old island.


young
scene y_name
when topic=travel
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : When my feet take stairs in pairs the missed step is an island.
b : Who lives there? | Does it have water?
a : Nobody unless I come back down and put a toe on it. | If the stair's wet all round it, yes. Mostly the water's pretend.

scene y_chalk
when topic=day self.job=child
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I've enough chalk for three tiny maps in my lesson book.
b : Are they real? | Only three?
a : #isle.capitalize# is real enough to hit a knee on. | I write small and use the corners nobody else looks at.

scene y_fish
when topic=food self.likes=fried_fish
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : The tail's the crunchiest flag on a plate of fish.
b : A flag? | Do you wave it?
a : I hold it by one end and it stands up. | Only before I eat it. A flag's not much use once it's crunched.

scene y_fog
when topic=weather self.likes=misty_dawns
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : In morning mist the top step might go anywhere.
b : Where would you like it to go? | Do you jump to find out?
a : A landing just big enough for me and a warm breakfast. | I feel for the wall first. A surprise oughtn't to cost my knees.

scene y_mud
when topic=travel self.dislikes=deep_mud
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : Mud pulls harder if I jump straight up.
b : Who wins? | What do you do?
a : It got a shoe once. I got the shoe back with two hands. | I lean onto the firm toe and turn the other foot sideways.

scene y_salt
when topic=weather self.dislikes=salt_wind
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : Salt on my lip spoils pretending I'm miles inland.
b : Could you pretend harder? | How far inland?
a : Not and lick my nose at the same time. | To a big dry hill with no wind blown off the water.

scene y_bells
when topic=festival self.likes=festival_bells
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : When the feast bell starts I pick the nearest island to stand on.
b : Can you stand still that long? | What for?
a : If I take a breath for each ring. The little quick ones don't count. | To feel the sound through my feet as well as inside my ears.

scene y_road
when topic=pastimes self.likes=long_walks
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I can go a long way with nowhere particular at the end.
b : How do you know you got there? | Does it get lonely?
a : I get hungry and turn round. That's a decent end. | Not when I keep noticing different corners.

scene y_study
when topic=work self.job=child self.workplace
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : At #self.workplace# I picture the spaces between numbers as steps.
b : What about a big number? | Does it help?
a : I take it in twos and give the odd one a whole landing. | Mostly. Till I draw one on the slate and must wipe it off before anyone sees.

scene y_shoulder
when topic=health
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : If I tuck one shoulder in my bag stops bouncing.
b : Doesn't it slip off? | Can you jump like that?
a : The strap sits against the base of my neck. That's firm. | I can. Sometimes my chalk doesn't care for the landing.

scene y_quarrel
when topic=dreams
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I worry the big Houses might stop speaking across the hill.
b : Did you hear a quarrel? | What if they did?
a : No. That's the worrying part, how readily my head invents one. | I'd need an island that didn't make me pick a side.

scene y_feed
when topic=home
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : There's a spot for a fish parcel on the flat of my knees.
b : Doesn't the butter run? | What if you stand up?
a : Hold the paper corners up. Tiny pond for my supper, all for me. | I finish the parcel first. That's hardly a difficult job.

story y_smudge [topic=memories]
  : I drew a chalk island on a scrap and tucked it beside my fish copper.
  : When the coin came out its edge had printed a little harbour all round my island.
  b : Did you spend the harbour?
  : I spent the fish money. The harbour stayed on the paper and I got both.


adolescent
scene t_jump
when topic=travel
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I used to miss the middle of every flight on purpose.
b : Do you go slowly now? | Did the steps have names?
a : When somebody's beside me. A companion might have shorter legs. | Only the skipped ones. I still remember a surprising number.

scene t_calm
when topic=friends
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I can keep two paces going by listening instead of talking.
b : Yours and whose? | What does it change?
a : Mine and whoever's walking with me. We find a comfortable third one. | I used to hear only whether I was ahead. Now I hear if someone's tired.

scene t_errand
when topic=day
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : A long errand gives me time to inspect old chalk marks.
b : Yours? | Can you tell how old?
a : If there's a little island in the margin of a step, probably mine. | Only that rain's had several goes at them. I like the faint ones best.

story t_mist [topic=memories]
  : I once went up a flight in mist and expected a very grand view once I made the top landing.
  : Instead I stood level with a gutter full of little beads of water. Every bead had its own tiny upside-down house.
  b : Had you gone far enough?
  : For that view, yes. Another stair would have lost me the whole street.
